# TypeScript

- Keep strict typing enabled.
- Use discriminated unions for commands, events, worker messages, and result states.
- Parse `unknown` at boundaries; do not cast external data into trust.
- Avoid `any`, broad `as`, `@ts-ignore`, non-null assertions, and catch-all index signatures.
- Prefer small named domain types and explicit return types on exported functions.
- Do not use TypeScript enums in data formats; use `as const` values and unions.
- Separate definition types, mutable instance types, and read models.
- Errors crossing package/worker boundaries are serializable structured objects.
- Exhaustively handle command/event unions with a `never` check.
